  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $855M in contracts in FY2027 to date. The Department of Health and Human Services recorded 1,971 awards with an average award size of $434K. The Department of Health and Human Services obligations fell 96.6% year over year. The Department of Health and Human Services obligations by fiscal year were $33.4B in FY22, $33.4B in FY23, $29.9B in FY24, $21.3B in FY25, $24.9B in FY26, and $855M in FY27. The Department of Health and Human Services spending in FY2027 to date is concentrated in a handful of NAICS categories. The Department of Health and Human Services allocated $128M to Computer Systems Design Services, $76M to Other Computer Related Services, $66.9M to Facilities Support Services, $65.2M to All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services, and $60.3M to Custom Computer Programming Services. The Department of Health and Human Services top vendors in FY2027 to date include SOFTRAMS LLC at $61.9M and GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. at $52.6M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does spending in FY2027 to date compare with prior years?",
        "body": "The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $855M in FY2027 to date, compared with $24.9B in FY26 and $33.4B in FY22 and FY23. The Department of Health and Human Services obligations fell 96.6% year over year. The Department of Health and Human Services recorded 1,971 awards in FY2027 to date with an average award size of $434K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which contract categories and vendors account for most FY2027 to date obligations?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services is the largest category at $128M, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $76M and Facilities Support Services at $66.9M. SOFTRAMS LLC is the top vendor at $61.9M, GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. is second at $52.6M, and FOUR SEASONS ENVIRONMENTAL INC is third at $49.3M."
      }
    ]
